      "message": "Index here is differenet from id, where `id` referes to an indentifer for an IOMMU which is defined by the driver, this used to have a way to identify IOMMUs between the kernel and the hypervisor (to be used for hypercalls)\n\nAnd idx is an actual index to one of the endpoints of a device connected to an IOMMU. This is used to hide the actual value of an endpoint from userspace and instead use index instead (similar to how KVM deals with irqs)",
